<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Rule Examples</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present two rules to illustrate KARI’s tree structure. <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pierce_through</span> (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) shows three alternative physical pathways, each scoped to a specific part. <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">fold_flat</span> (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>) shows four alternatives that all describe the whole object.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="LST1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">Rule for <span id="LST1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">pierce_through</span>.</p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
